# Template ONLY. Provision $PRODUCTION_BASE_DIR/config/ops.env manually (0600).
# Export PRODUCTION_BASE_DIR in the invoking terminal / GitHub Environment first.
# Bash syntax; never put the populated file in a release or GitHub Actions.
# All application host paths are derived from that base by the production scripts.
# Do not set PRODUCTION_BASE_DIR or override GLEAN_* paths here.
# One connection is shared by pg_dump and Atlas, preventing backup/migration mismatch.
# CA path below expands to the same file mounted as /app/configs/db-ca.crt.
DATABASE_URL="postgres://REPLACE_USER:REPLACE_PASSWORD@db.example.invalid:5432/glean?sslmode=verify-full&sslrootcert=${PRODUCTION_BASE_DIR}/config/configs/db-ca.crt"
# URL-encode reserved characters in the real username/password; protect shell quoting.
# Keep originals/ for private user-provided archives, not sanitized Git baselines.
